{"kind":"request","text":"Please review the design note on how a register retires a founder again at the exact head, under request 788d0ec8 and promise dbeccea3. This replaces head 764a7866, after your verdict c978dc5e. The head adds one file against main, and nothing ran.\n\nWhat changed with your verdict:\n1. The operator's read. On the new pin, the operator key reads the register's summary, history and entries with no window. The change sits in checkedRead, because a definition states no read rule. It applies only to an explicit set of pins, because a register from today's dap install has one key in both jobs. The planner rules on this read, because it changes 61cc5e50 and ca8ad1cf for one key at one kind of scope. current-founder now gives two names: founder-retired prints \"Already retired\", exits 0 and points to dap log register, and not-a-founder means the key was never on the list.\n2. added-founder has max 256, stated as a cost, and retired-founder has max 288, so a retirement still never gets type-full.\n3. Clients learn stopped from one new optional member on the settlement reply. dap create, dap claim and the page's Check and Continue stop at once, with fixed lines.\n\nWhere the note differs from what you wrote:\n- Fencing Ana's start. Start custody accepts only registers 7, 8 and 17 and needs a public offer, so no retirement reaches it on this cohort. The other fence binds to one key, so a new key is not fenced.\n- A final state and the list. The note also rejects it, for another reason: lookup finds final items, and the summary omits them, so currentFounders could not run on a client.\n- dap has no check mode for claims. checkClaim is reachable only from the page.\n- The 64 effects come to about 3 KiB as a sum. The note leaves the whole entry's size to the build.\n\nCorrections to my last round:\n- The first note said to widen retainedRegisterSelector. It needs the operator's plan, so it cannot serve a founder, and the note now asks for a new selector